<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-013>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-013" ;
  triage:title "colima_skill_report write_report/render never wired to the ancestor-fallback rule -- live 404 in committed evidence" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BB3-QA3-1789250000 (Final verdict FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1445#issuecomment-5648698551, 2026-09-12T21:08:20Z; BB3-QA3-B1), reviewed at 66be1d012. write_report/colima_skill_report.render (scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py:822-827, scripts/smoke/colima_skill_report.py:90-104) build procedure_href from the exact source_revision() short SHA with no ancestor fallback, unlike .just/generate_report_index.py's resolve_procedures/_revision_is_ancestor. Confirmed as a live 404 in currently-committed evidence: site/reports/smoke/macos/rand-m5.local/20260912T204119754750Z-pid87697-fast/index.html:18 links to procedures/smoke-fast/fe5dac5c.html, which does not exist (site/reports/procedures/smoke-fast/ has only 513b3374, 7475fed9, 8043ce64, 93458691, c355f382, index). Verified this file is tracked and committed in d938673e4, not stale/uncommitted output. Violates AC2 and D5's report-header contract. A regression adjacent to BB3-003's fix: the index-generator's own ancestor resolution is genuinely fixed and tested, but the per-run report's self-embedded link was never wired to the same rule." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py,scripts/smoke/colima_skill_report.py" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T21:08:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Fix: resolve procedure_href via the same exact-then-ancestor rule (or a shared helper) in both write_report and colima_skill_report.render, with a regression test asserting the linked file exists on disk. Routed to solar's BB3-FIX-R3-1789253000 (fenix, promote_to_branch fix/bb3-qa3-r3, queued behind BB1-FIX-R1). cipher's BB3-FIX-R4-1789255000 (task event 2026-09-12T23:08:15Z) reported this not-reproducible at the current, already-satisfied path on fix/bb3-qa3-r4 @ f94125cf5 (PR #1455, includes merges of #1456 d1969185f and #1453 1c7e76da5); just lint 36/36, just test exit 0, just smoke fast 8/8. Fixed-pending-QA (verify-not-reproducible); QA dispatched as BB3-QA4-1789262000 on PR #1455 (queued behind BB5-QA-R1) to confirm against the record. STILL OPEN (BB3-QA4-1789262000, PR #1455 comment, 2026-09-12T23:24:52Z, blocking): the specific reported 404 is gone, but the fix wired both call sites to a NEW third implementation (scripts/report_runtime.py::resolve_procedure_page) that itself diverges from .just/generate_report_index.py's own resolver -- report_runtime.py takes the first ancestor match in manifest order and raises on any non-0/1 git exit code, while generate_report_index.py detects git-unavailability and falls back to the newest entry dated <= generated_at, otherwise picks the max-by-date ancestor. Two implementations of 'the same rule' still exist and can select different pages for the same envelope under the exact failure modes that produced the original 404. Next: cut a new layer above fix/bb3-qa3-r4 (top of stack #1457) making resolve_procedure_page share the exact same ancestor-resolution implementation as generate_report_index.py (one calls the other, or extract one shared function both call), including the missing git-unavailable dated-fallback branch. Corrected routing (fenix, 2026-09-12T23:32:13Z): the fix layer is fix/bb3-qa4-r5, cut from a7d4664d1 (feature/bb6-storage-prompt-handoffs, top of stack #1457) -- not directly above fix/bb3-qa3-r4. In the BB3-FIX-R5-1789264000 fence, closes on cipher's fix." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "BB3-003" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T21:08:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-013/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-013/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-013/3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "4" .

